NAME
    impact - the units a change can affect, with the rule and the file

SYNOPSIS
    impact [--base REV] [--head REV] [--tier T] [--depth N] [--repo DIR]
    impact --explain FILE [--tier T]
    impact --base REV --head REV --blast FILE

DESCRIPTION
    A command of the emusen.testing module. It reads the files that
    differ between the merge base of --base (default WiseMan) and --head
    (default HEAD, with the working tree's uncommitted changes) and prints
    one line per unit, tab-separated:

        kind    unit    reason    via

    kind is cargo or dotnet; unit a crate folder or a test class's full
    name; reason the rule that chose it; via the file that brought it.
    The rules, in order, the first reason for a unit kept:

        recording  a changed recording (a line of kind 'recording' in
                   Testing/inputs.json) selects its owner; a file ending
                   as a recording does (.spec, .golden, ...) that no line
                   owns selects the tier's whole set
        always     a test class's own file selects the class; a unit that
                   failed in this branch's last trial is selected again
        declared   a folder line of Testing/inputs.json adds its units,
                   and narrows a reached test project to them
        graph      the file's owner (its nearest crate or project, or the
                   project that imports it) and everything in its reverse
                   closure over Cargo path dependencies, workspaces,
                   ProjectReference and Import, and the host's crate edges
                   (RustCores.props, Platform.targets); a test project the
                   closure reaches and no line narrows is selected whole
        closed     a file no rule claims selects the tier's whole set:
                   unknown is closed, never open

    A line of kind 'none' (documentation, ignore lists, CI files) claims a
    file and selects nothing. A tier's named_only classes (WindowFitAudit-
    Tests at land) are selected only by a line naming them; its excluded
    tags (nightly) are left out. --depth limits the reverse closure, as
    the fast tier does with 1.

    --explain FILE prints the file's owner, what its closure reaches, the
    lines it matches and its selection. --blast FILE compares the
    selection with what blast.sh printed for the same revisions: each
    unit as 'agree', 'impact' (impact only) or 'blast' (blast.sh only),
    blast.sh's filter terms resolved to classes under its own exclusions,
    its unmapped files, and a summary line. land.sh logs this while the
    two run side by side.

    Terms that name no class are reported on standard error. See
    EmuSen_Testing.md §3.2 and §6.

EXAMPLES
    impact
    impact --base WiseMan --head approve-fix --tier land
    impact | grep -c '^dotnet'
    impact --explain EmuSen.Mistress/Views/CoresWindow.axaml.cs
    impact --base f1592d39e^1 --head f1592d39e^2 --blast blast.txt | grep -v ^agree
